WEBVTT

00:56.264 --> 00:59.517
I should go... Now...

01:08.651 --> 01:10.111
This is so strange.

01:11.237 --> 01:13.865
Ms. Ko Mun-yeong told me
to come over with you,

01:14.574 --> 01:16.034
but she's not here.

01:16.534 --> 01:18.328
Mun-yeong?

01:18.912 --> 01:19.871
Mun-yeong...

01:21.998 --> 01:24.000
I wonder if she and Gang-tae
have made up yet.

01:24.084 --> 01:26.753
Have they made up...

01:29.422 --> 01:31.674
This means I have to change my plan.

01:36.054 --> 01:39.808
It'll be more fun to put both you
and Mun-yeong to sleep together.

01:39.891 --> 01:42.852
I guess they kissed...

01:45.563 --> 01:46.940
My gosh, you're so cute.

01:49.818 --> 01:52.946
Don't touch it. Don't touch my hair!

01:53.029 --> 01:54.656
Don't touch my hair.

01:54.739 --> 01:57.158
Don't touch... Don't touch my hair.

01:57.575 --> 01:59.536
Goodness.

01:59.619 --> 02:03.581
What do I do...

02:05.708 --> 02:06.835
Gosh.

02:14.092 --> 02:16.594
MY BROTHER

02:23.476 --> 02:25.061
SANG-TAE

02:25.645 --> 02:27.272
- Sang-tae, where are you--
- Oh, Mr. Moon.

02:33.945 --> 02:36.781
You're always looking for your brother.

02:37.740 --> 02:38.741
Sang-tae.

02:39.784 --> 02:40.785
Sang-tae.

02:41.452 --> 02:43.288
Sang-tae.

02:43.496 --> 02:44.497
Sang-tae!

02:47.333 --> 02:48.376
Where can I meet you?

02:52.422 --> 02:53.631
The cursed castle.

02:58.928 --> 03:04.726
CHAPTER 15
A TALE OF TWO BROTHERS

03:58.821 --> 03:59.697
Sang-tae.

04:02.242 --> 04:03.243
Sang-tae.

04:04.035 --> 04:05.161
Sang-tae!

04:05.828 --> 04:06.913
Sang-tae.

04:13.086 --> 04:14.712
Why are you looking at me like that?

04:15.463 --> 04:17.173
You look as if
you want to rip me to pieces.

04:18.466 --> 04:19.300
I like that.

04:19.884 --> 04:21.302
What did you do to Sang-tae?

04:24.222 --> 04:25.890
Don't worry. I didn't kill him.

04:26.766 --> 04:29.394
I gave him a tranquilizer,
so he'll wake up soon.

04:30.270 --> 04:31.854
But it's too bad.

04:32.272 --> 04:33.731
Mun-yeong should've been here, too.

04:33.856 --> 04:37.235
I really wanted to see
which one of them you'd choose.

04:39.153 --> 04:41.781
- Did you hide her somewhere?
- Why are you doing this?

04:43.032 --> 04:44.242
Why are you doing this to us?

04:45.451 --> 04:47.787
Because you ruined my daughter.

04:48.663 --> 04:51.791
- What?
- She was my most perfect artwork,

04:52.375 --> 04:54.043
but she's changed because of you.

04:55.295 --> 04:56.129
Is your daughter...

04:59.465 --> 05:00.675
an artwork to you?

05:04.304 --> 05:05.638
We don't look alike at all, right?

05:06.222 --> 05:08.224
I went under the knife
so I wouldn't look like her,

05:08.308 --> 05:10.601
but she got those facial features from me.

05:11.519 --> 05:15.356
That face and that body.
Her hair and even her soul.

05:15.565 --> 05:19.902
I molded her. I created her.
She's my work of art.

05:21.738 --> 05:24.949
Mun-yeong doesn't belong to you.

05:26.951 --> 05:28.536
She's a person, not a piece of art.

05:29.203 --> 05:30.413
She's a human being!

05:33.541 --> 05:35.126
Damn it.

05:37.253 --> 05:40.715
She won't listen to me because of you!

05:41.966 --> 05:44.552
All failures must be discarded.

05:50.600 --> 05:52.518
I don't want to do that

05:52.852 --> 05:54.520
because of all the hard work I've done.

05:55.313 --> 05:57.065
I'll give you a chance instead.

05:57.482 --> 05:59.108
Take your brother and run far away.

05:59.776 --> 06:02.028
As far away as you can go from Mun-yeong.

06:02.862 --> 06:03.821
No.

06:04.572 --> 06:05.990
I'll never do that.

06:08.326 --> 06:09.660
I knew you'd say that.

06:10.244 --> 06:12.997
Then here's another option for you.

06:16.584 --> 06:17.877
Kill me.

06:19.921 --> 06:22.548
If you kill me, you'll get your revenge.

06:23.424 --> 06:24.592
And when Mun-yeong sees

06:24.675 --> 06:26.719
that you killed me,
she'll get her old self back.

06:26.803 --> 06:29.639
Then the two of you will never get out
of your ill-fated relationship.

06:30.973 --> 06:31.808
So,

06:33.935 --> 06:35.520
this was the ending

06:37.021 --> 06:37.855
that you wanted?

06:37.939 --> 06:39.273
Correct!

06:41.692 --> 06:44.487
A happy ending for everyone.

06:50.201 --> 06:51.035
Give it up.

06:52.036 --> 06:53.079
What?

06:53.162 --> 06:55.206
That messed up ending you're dreaming of

06:56.415 --> 06:57.416
will never come.

06:58.543 --> 07:00.044
- Because I will never
- Gosh.

07:02.338 --> 07:03.965
give up on Mun-yeong.

07:07.844 --> 07:10.555
Even though your mother died
because of Mun-yeong?

07:11.514 --> 07:14.058
Do you want to hear the story?
It's very interesting.

07:27.655 --> 07:29.782
This is where I met your mother
for the first time.

07:39.333 --> 07:41.586
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST

07:54.682 --> 07:55.683
Excuse me.

07:56.684 --> 07:57.727
Hello.

07:58.227 --> 08:00.062
The employment agency sent me here
for the job--

08:00.229 --> 08:02.190
Okay, then do the work.

08:03.649 --> 08:04.650
Yes, ma'am.

08:05.651 --> 08:06.694
Thank you.

08:39.393 --> 08:42.146
Hey, what are you doing over there?

08:51.113 --> 08:54.992
A bird with a broken wing
can't fly anyway.

08:55.660 --> 08:56.661
What?

08:59.455 --> 09:00.665
I should kill it, right?

09:21.060 --> 09:23.938
She said since the bird can't fly anyway,

09:25.022 --> 09:26.607
it'd be better just to kill it.

09:29.860 --> 09:30.987
I'm proud of her.

09:33.573 --> 09:34.699
Well...

09:35.241 --> 09:37.994
There's this hospital
my elder son goes to.

09:39.829 --> 09:40.830
Excuse me.

09:42.290 --> 09:43.124
Yes, ma'am?

09:45.334 --> 09:46.627
Thank you for your hard work.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.216
Oh, okay.

10:39.764 --> 10:40.931
Mom...

10:48.439 --> 10:49.523
That's it?

10:51.901 --> 10:53.235
That's why

10:55.029 --> 10:56.238
you killed her?

11:01.869 --> 11:02.953
Because of

11:04.830 --> 11:06.165
what she said?

11:11.504 --> 11:14.340
That's why you killed my mom?

11:21.430 --> 11:23.891
She talked as if
my daughter was a lunatic.

11:25.935 --> 11:27.395
How dare she.

11:36.195 --> 11:38.364
Yes, kill me.

11:42.118 --> 11:43.619
Don't...

11:45.621 --> 11:47.331
Don't ever become weak.

11:58.092 --> 11:59.260
But you know,

12:00.302 --> 12:01.512
she is

12:04.348 --> 12:05.850
still my mom.

12:29.665 --> 12:31.417
Gosh, you're such a coward.

12:42.720 --> 12:44.972
This is why I don't like people
who are weak.

12:48.559 --> 12:52.980
But Mun-yeong and I
are different from you guys.

12:53.689 --> 12:54.523
Get that?

12:59.153 --> 13:00.529
Stop talking bullshit.

13:04.950 --> 13:06.535
There you are.

13:08.078 --> 13:09.538
Denying it is useless

13:10.247 --> 13:12.791
because you and I share the same blood.

13:12.875 --> 13:13.709
No.

13:15.503 --> 13:18.297
I'm not a monster like you!

13:28.057 --> 13:30.935
Even if the butterfly shows up,

13:31.810 --> 13:33.145
do not kill it.

13:34.188 --> 13:35.439
You shouldn't.

13:37.775 --> 13:38.609
You

13:40.319 --> 13:41.570
promised me.

13:44.031 --> 13:45.074
That you wouldn't do this.

13:55.626 --> 13:56.460
Hey.

13:57.795 --> 13:59.046
What's wrong with you?

13:59.797 --> 14:00.923
Wake up.

14:02.258 --> 14:03.217
Moon Gang-tae.

14:04.301 --> 14:06.345
Moon Gang-tae, wake up.

14:07.221 --> 14:08.347
Moon Gang-tae!

14:08.931 --> 14:12.726
Did you think you'd be able
to escape from me by cutting your hair?

14:13.394 --> 14:14.478
Wake up.

14:15.354 --> 14:17.481
Please wake up, Moon Gang-tae--

14:19.066 --> 14:20.276
I told you so!

14:23.112 --> 14:27.032
You should've listened to Mom.

14:27.616 --> 14:29.702
My daughter, my baby.

14:30.786 --> 14:31.787
My baby.

14:48.262 --> 14:50.222
Don't hurt my brother and sister.

14:50.306 --> 14:52.683
Don't hurt my brother and sister!

15:34.475 --> 15:40.314
THE WORLD'S BEST FAIRY TALES

15:44.944 --> 15:46.779
My gosh, thank you.

15:52.743 --> 15:54.203
Goodness.

15:56.246 --> 15:59.708
It looks like someone smacked you hard
on the head.

16:02.920 --> 16:06.507
Don't get too excited. I won.

16:08.217 --> 16:10.719
Those two can't be together.

16:11.512 --> 16:12.972
I made sure of it.

16:13.555 --> 16:15.391
We don't know that yet.

16:15.474 --> 16:16.517
You're wrong.

16:17.267 --> 16:18.560
Humans

16:20.145 --> 16:21.438
are too weak.

16:23.148 --> 16:27.236
That's why they suffer,
like your patients.

16:28.070 --> 16:29.154
Haeng-ja.

16:30.906 --> 16:33.784
People stick together
because they're weak.

16:42.501 --> 16:43.836
We lean on each other like this.

16:45.629 --> 16:47.923
That's what makes us human.

16:49.883 --> 16:51.385
Will you ever be human?

16:55.305 --> 16:56.515
Let's go.

17:12.156 --> 17:13.907
What on earth did you do to Park Ok-ran?

17:16.285 --> 17:17.703
Oh, that woman.

17:20.372 --> 17:22.124
She was such a great actress.

17:36.555 --> 17:39.433
Walk down the hallway at dawn

17:40.851 --> 17:43.771
while singing "Oh My Darling, Clementine."

17:47.066 --> 17:50.027
Visit Do Hui-jae's castle at night

17:50.444 --> 17:52.946
and wish Mun-yeong a happy birthday.

17:57.034 --> 17:58.702
Go to the study

17:58.786 --> 18:01.955
and leave the envelope with the butterfly
on the desk.

18:16.512 --> 18:20.682
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST 9

18:20.766 --> 18:22.434
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST 9

18:24.895 --> 18:26.021
Ms. Park Ok-ran.

18:35.572 --> 18:38.617
The show's over now,
so she should leave the stage.

18:42.788 --> 18:46.208
Maybe she's putting on a different show
elsewhere.

18:51.171 --> 18:54.383
It's about time
you left the stage as well.

18:55.968 --> 18:57.010
Please get going.

19:16.071 --> 19:17.406
Is he really just asleep?

19:18.699 --> 19:19.992
He'll wake up, right?

19:20.784 --> 19:21.618
Why?

19:22.786 --> 19:24.037
If he never wakes up,

19:24.663 --> 19:26.665
will you take your own life
like Romeo did?

19:27.791 --> 19:28.959
He may never wake up?

19:31.587 --> 19:33.672
He fainted because he got
high doses of Ativan.

19:34.173 --> 19:36.675
But I've given him some fluid,
so he'll wake up in a few hours.

19:36.758 --> 19:38.051
Don't worry too much.

20:09.374 --> 20:12.586
Is he okay? Is my little brother okay?

20:12.669 --> 20:16.048
Yes. He's just asleep,
so don't worry too much.

20:16.632 --> 20:19.343
The head nurse is really horrible.
She's a horrible person.

20:19.426 --> 20:22.846
She tried to hurt my siblings
and lied to me.

20:22.971 --> 20:25.599
She even tried to touch
the back of my head.

20:25.682 --> 20:27.017
I'm glad you taught her a lesson.

20:27.559 --> 20:29.937
You saved their lives, Sang-tae.

20:30.562 --> 20:32.231
I'm truly proud of you.

20:32.898 --> 20:35.859
I saved them. I did it.

20:35.943 --> 20:40.864
I saved them.
That's right. I saved their lives.

20:51.041 --> 20:52.251
You get hurt

20:55.087 --> 20:56.713
because of me every single time.

21:00.467 --> 21:01.551
I'm sorry.

21:05.889 --> 21:07.015
I'm sorry.

21:08.350 --> 21:09.685
Denying it is useless

21:10.269 --> 21:12.437
because you and I share the same blood.

21:16.316 --> 21:17.484
If you stay with me,

21:20.862 --> 21:22.614
your life will be miserable.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.201
I'm sorry.

21:49.057 --> 21:52.102
- Pick up, please.
- The number you have dialed is not...

21:52.602 --> 21:55.188
Gosh, this is driving me nuts.

21:55.814 --> 21:59.151
Why isn't anyone picking up?
What if something terrible happened?

21:59.651 --> 22:01.570
Damn it. This is driving me nuts.

22:04.614 --> 22:06.700
Hey, you're here for questioning.
What's with this attitude?

22:06.783 --> 22:08.076
I'm really sorry.

22:08.160 --> 22:11.455
Someone I know
is in an urgent situation at the moment.

22:11.538 --> 22:13.040
Please excuse me for a moment.

22:13.582 --> 22:15.167
Look who's talking.

22:15.250 --> 22:17.252
You can't afford
to worry about someone else now.

22:17.336 --> 22:21.048
You crossed the centerline
and made an illegal U-turn.

22:21.131 --> 22:22.424
When you were told to stop,

22:22.507 --> 22:25.761
you kept speeding and almost hit a deer!

22:25.844 --> 22:26.970
Gosh, seriously!

22:27.054 --> 22:30.057
Who cares about that darn deer now?

22:30.140 --> 22:32.350
Someone might die!

22:32.434 --> 22:35.270
- Mr. Lee!
- Hey, Seung-jae.

22:36.438 --> 22:37.564
What happened?

22:38.148 --> 22:39.232
Ju-ri.

22:41.693 --> 22:43.737
You made an illegal U-turn,
went over the speed limit,

22:43.820 --> 22:46.615
ran away, and almost killed a deer?

22:46.698 --> 22:49.367
That sounds like an NIS agent
in an intense car chase.

22:49.701 --> 22:52.287
What the heck were you doing
all by yourself?

22:52.370 --> 22:54.456
Jeez, it's none of your business.

22:55.123 --> 22:56.583
Ju-ri, spare me a moment.

23:00.921 --> 23:03.507
Are Gang-tae and Mun-yeong really okay?

23:03.882 --> 23:04.800
Are you sure?

23:05.383 --> 23:07.094
Yes, Jae-su called

23:07.177 --> 23:09.638
and told me that they're fine.
He told me not to worry.

23:11.640 --> 23:13.141
What's going on?

23:13.725 --> 23:14.559
Ju-ri.

23:16.394 --> 23:20.232
I think for some people, it's just
really hard to live a normal life.

23:22.609 --> 23:26.571
It feels like some mean god's
sent all kinds of misfortune their way.

23:27.739 --> 23:30.450
I feel so bad for them,
and it makes me upset

23:31.827 --> 23:33.328
and furious.

23:36.540 --> 23:38.333
The law of
the total number of misfortunes.

23:39.417 --> 23:42.796
I heard we all have a set amount of
happiness and misfortune assigned to us.

23:43.505 --> 23:45.924
If their lives have been filled
with misfortune up till now,

23:46.675 --> 23:48.552
it means only happiness awaits them.

23:50.846 --> 23:52.347
I really hope that's the case.

23:59.604 --> 24:01.940
Gross, that was so cheesy.

24:03.525 --> 24:05.318
I want to down a glass of soda.

24:06.653 --> 24:08.697
Then when I woke up,

24:08.780 --> 24:12.534
I saw the mean head nurse
grabbing Mun-yeong by the hair

24:12.617 --> 24:15.328
and trying to stab Gang-tae
with the pen with her other hand--

24:15.412 --> 24:18.373
- She tried to stab him. You got all angry
- Yes, so...

24:18.456 --> 24:21.793
and hit her on the back of her head
with the book.

24:21.877 --> 24:24.963
In conclusion, the brave Sang-tae
saved Mun-yeong and Gang-tae's lives.

24:25.046 --> 24:27.257
I've heard the story eight times,
so I have it memorized.

24:28.717 --> 24:30.719
Right. You're proud of me, right?

24:31.595 --> 24:32.679
Are you proud of me?

24:35.640 --> 24:36.474
I am, of course.

24:38.435 --> 24:40.520
You rock. You're the best.

24:40.604 --> 24:43.231
- You're the best.
- The best! I'm the best!

24:46.943 --> 24:49.321
Anyhow, I ran here
because I was worried about him.

24:49.404 --> 24:52.365
Is he Sleeping Beauty or what?
When the heck will he wake up?

24:52.449 --> 24:54.618
- A kiss!
- What?

24:55.493 --> 24:58.413
Only the prince's kiss
can wake Sleeping Beauty.

24:58.496 --> 24:59.623
That's right, a kiss.

25:02.125 --> 25:04.127
- So from behind, I smacked...
- Smack!

26:12.153 --> 26:13.113
Did you sleep well?

26:14.906 --> 26:15.740
Yes.

26:18.910 --> 26:20.120
I think I slept for too long.

26:21.204 --> 26:22.956
I had a really long dream,

26:25.166 --> 26:26.584
and it was a terrible nightmare.

26:34.551 --> 26:35.552
It wasn't a dream.

26:38.054 --> 26:39.014
Come downstairs.

26:40.432 --> 26:41.308
We need to talk.

27:12.380 --> 27:14.007
Now do you see?

27:20.055 --> 27:22.098
It actually happened right here.

27:23.600 --> 27:25.393
Just a few hours ago.

27:33.568 --> 27:36.946
Please wake up, Moon Gang-tae. Wake up!

27:37.530 --> 27:38.573
It's all over now.

27:40.617 --> 27:41.826
We're alive,

27:43.036 --> 27:43.870
and my mom...

27:48.416 --> 27:49.918
That woman was arrested.

27:51.544 --> 27:53.671
And the truth will be revealed soon.

27:59.803 --> 28:00.720
Please leave.

28:05.475 --> 28:06.559
Leave this place.

28:08.103 --> 28:10.730
Like you said, I'm not an empty can.

28:11.439 --> 28:12.732
I have feelings too,

28:14.776 --> 28:16.486
so I will never forget

28:18.196 --> 28:21.241
the terrible things you and Sang-tae
had to experience here because of me.

28:22.367 --> 28:23.827
They'll stay with me forever.

28:26.079 --> 28:27.163
And you'll probably

28:28.123 --> 28:29.833
suffer emotionally every time you see me.

28:36.423 --> 28:37.549
We won't forget any of it.

28:39.676 --> 28:41.094
We'll overcome it.

28:42.595 --> 28:43.555
You said that's

28:45.140 --> 28:46.433
the only way we can become

28:47.726 --> 28:49.018
real adults whose souls can grow.

28:53.273 --> 28:54.357
We should just...

28:56.901 --> 28:58.695
Let's just think of it as a nightmare.

29:02.532 --> 29:03.742
I can do it.

29:07.704 --> 29:09.205
Stop pretending.

29:11.166 --> 29:12.751
Stop pretending like it doesn't hurt.

29:13.501 --> 29:15.170
Stop pretending like you're okay.

29:15.754 --> 29:16.921
Pretending to be okay...

29:19.507 --> 29:20.759
You're going to do it

29:21.718 --> 29:23.344
in front of me. Not just Sang-tae.

29:24.763 --> 29:26.890
And seeing that masked face

29:28.308 --> 29:30.310
will make me walk on eggshells around you.

29:31.603 --> 29:32.854
It'll suffocate me.

29:33.897 --> 29:35.482
I'll be tormented.

29:39.402 --> 29:40.612
I don't want to live like that.

29:42.155 --> 29:43.531
That's why I'm asking you to leave.

29:45.825 --> 29:47.660
Move out tomorrow with Sang-tae.

29:57.253 --> 29:58.087
Mun-yeong.

30:02.008 --> 30:03.343
Do you really mean it?

30:07.263 --> 30:08.264
Yes.

30:09.224 --> 30:11.017
I just want to live alone.

30:12.018 --> 30:13.061
Like I used to.

30:49.764 --> 30:51.307
You did well, Mun-yeong.

30:53.935 --> 30:55.019
You did well.

31:28.094 --> 31:29.762
Why do both of you look so tired?

31:30.722 --> 31:32.056
Did you not get much sleep last night?

31:32.140 --> 31:34.934
- I had to think about--
- Something came up last night.

31:37.520 --> 31:38.479
By any chance,

31:39.314 --> 31:43.651
did Ms. Ko and Mr. Moon
get into a fight last night or something?

31:45.653 --> 31:49.324
Well, you ended up
at the police station last night, Mr. Lee.

31:50.158 --> 31:52.201
And Jae-su,
you closed the restaurant early

31:52.285 --> 31:54.370
and ran to Ms. Ko's studio.

31:55.538 --> 31:58.875
Doesn't that mean
something crazy happened there?

31:59.459 --> 32:01.169
- Is that right?
- Is it true?

32:05.214 --> 32:06.299
No, not at all.

32:06.507 --> 32:09.052
They did get into a heated argument, but--

32:09.135 --> 32:12.472
Right, they reconciled quickly.

32:12.555 --> 32:17.352
Gosh. Mun-yeong not only has a bad temper,
but she's also very fussy.

32:17.435 --> 32:20.104
She's a hard one to please.

32:20.355 --> 32:24.359
Mr. Moon must be having a hard time.

32:24.442 --> 32:26.903
Gosh, you obviously don't know him well.

32:26.986 --> 32:29.197
He's like a nine-tailed fox.

32:29.280 --> 32:30.823
He has a knack for gaining control

32:30.907 --> 32:32.742
over someone by charming the person.

32:32.825 --> 32:35.495
Tell Ms. Ko to be careful
because the fox might eat her liver.

32:35.578 --> 32:37.246
- Sure, of course.
- Okay?

32:38.373 --> 32:40.750
It sounds like the two of them
are meant to be.

32:40.833 --> 32:42.210
The soup will get cold. Eat up.

32:42.293 --> 32:43.419
- Okay.
- Okay.

32:44.671 --> 32:46.381
I think they're lying.

33:07.777 --> 33:08.778
Sang-tae.

33:11.823 --> 33:12.865
Sang-tae.

33:16.536 --> 33:17.870
Hey, are you okay?

33:18.162 --> 33:20.999
Are you all right?

33:23.793 --> 33:25.837
Did you... Did you get enough sleep?

33:27.922 --> 33:30.216
What about your hand?
Has it stopped bleeding?

33:30.299 --> 33:31.718
It doesn't hurt anymore?

33:32.802 --> 33:34.053
It hurts.

33:36.389 --> 33:37.640
It hurts so much that

33:38.725 --> 33:39.600
I feel like I'm dying.

33:39.684 --> 33:43.021
Oh, no. Then you need to go
to the hospital. The hospital.

33:50.278 --> 33:51.529
Thank you.

33:53.906 --> 33:54.991
Thank you for saving

33:55.908 --> 33:57.076
all of us.

33:59.996 --> 34:01.080
But...

34:03.166 --> 34:04.000
But...

34:05.334 --> 34:06.711
why did she do that?

34:09.422 --> 34:11.716
The head nurse was a nice person.

34:11.841 --> 34:14.469
Why did she do such a bad thing?

34:21.309 --> 34:22.477
That woman

34:24.479 --> 34:25.813
was a terrible person

34:26.731 --> 34:28.691
who just acted nice.

34:30.276 --> 34:31.235
She said

34:32.487 --> 34:36.449
she really hated the idea
of others becoming happy.

34:37.950 --> 34:39.577
The Murder of the Witch of the West.

34:40.745 --> 34:43.039
There's a story like that in that book.

34:43.122 --> 34:45.666
The female serial killer
who kills happy people.

34:45.750 --> 34:47.502
That is the Witch of the West.

34:48.795 --> 34:50.797
You read that book too?

34:50.880 --> 34:54.592
Yes. Someone left the book
at the hospital, so I read it.

34:55.760 --> 34:58.721
Not the whole book though.
Only up to page 63.

34:58.805 --> 35:00.973
But it's so boring. It's really boring.

35:03.976 --> 35:05.019
I see.

35:06.062 --> 35:07.647
It's a boring book, so don't read it.

35:08.856 --> 35:13.528
Is the head nurse
as horrible as the Witch of the West?

35:17.698 --> 35:18.658
Yes.

35:19.450 --> 35:23.621
But she gave me Dooly's mom as a gift.

35:25.832 --> 35:26.666
Then,

35:27.625 --> 35:29.544
what do I do with Dooly's mom now?

35:35.049 --> 35:37.426
I'll put it in the trash on my way out.

35:38.302 --> 35:39.470
Okay, throw it out.

35:43.808 --> 35:45.560
No, don't throw it out.

35:49.730 --> 35:52.733
Why not? A bad person gave it to you.
Let's just throw it out.

35:54.193 --> 35:57.071
No, Dooly's mom didn't do anything wrong.

35:57.363 --> 35:59.323
The person who gave it to me is bad,

35:59.407 --> 36:02.410
but Dooly's mom isn't.

36:02.493 --> 36:06.789
She... She didn't do anything wrong,
so don't throw her out. I won't let you.

36:08.875 --> 36:09.834
You're right.

36:11.627 --> 36:12.920
She didn't do anything wrong.

36:14.463 --> 36:15.882
She's not the bad one.

36:16.966 --> 36:21.387
I won't... I won't throw you out.

36:22.513 --> 36:24.807
You must've been scared.

36:24.891 --> 36:28.811
I'm sorry. I won't throw you out.
No way. I won't let it happen.

36:57.840 --> 36:59.050
Are you up?

37:00.343 --> 37:01.719
I made some soup,

37:02.303 --> 37:03.804
so eat it when you get hungry.

37:04.722 --> 37:06.140
I'm going to the hospital.

37:29.664 --> 37:30.498
Sang-tae.

37:31.791 --> 37:33.292
If Mun-yeong

37:36.796 --> 37:38.464
wants us to move out, what will you do?

37:42.635 --> 37:44.929
We're a family,
so we should live together.

37:46.931 --> 37:48.975
But what if she tells us to move out?

37:50.393 --> 37:52.061
We can move out.

37:52.144 --> 37:55.147
We should take Mun-yeong with us though.

38:00.152 --> 38:00.987
Why?

38:01.821 --> 38:05.157
Because she'll be left alone
if the two of us move out.

38:05.241 --> 38:06.742
If she's left all alone,

38:09.495 --> 38:10.579
she'll be bored.

38:11.372 --> 38:13.916
She always says that she's bored
and asks me to play with her.

38:19.922 --> 38:20.965
But what if

38:22.258 --> 38:24.343
she says that only the two of us
should move out?

38:28.180 --> 38:30.516
Over my dead body.

38:32.727 --> 38:36.480
We'll just say, "Over my dead body."
That will make us the winner.

38:36.564 --> 38:39.358
Over my dead body! We're going to win.

38:39.442 --> 38:41.319
Over my dead body. We're not moving out.

38:41.402 --> 38:44.322
Over my dead body.
We're not going anywhere.

38:44.405 --> 38:46.574
Over my dead body. We're not moving out.

38:46.657 --> 38:48.534
Over my dead body!

39:08.179 --> 39:10.473
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

39:11.057 --> 39:11.891
Why?

39:13.434 --> 39:15.519
Are you running away again
to a different hospital?

39:16.103 --> 39:16.937
No.

39:19.899 --> 39:21.400
I want to take it easy now.

39:22.568 --> 39:24.487
I guess we were thinking the same thing.

39:24.820 --> 39:27.615
I'm going to quit
so I can spend my time doing what I want.

39:28.991 --> 39:30.284
Shall we hang out together?

39:32.078 --> 39:33.746
I already have someone to hang out with.

39:33.829 --> 39:36.832
Can you at least act like you're torn?

39:39.418 --> 39:40.503
Are you

39:41.629 --> 39:45.049
resigning because of what happened?

39:46.008 --> 39:48.844
As the director, I should
take responsibility for what happened.

39:50.429 --> 39:52.556
I didn't know what was going on
right under my nose,

39:53.808 --> 39:56.727
so I don't think I can continue
to study the mind.

40:03.359 --> 40:04.193
Then,

40:07.822 --> 40:10.032
think of this as the last time.

40:11.409 --> 40:13.119
Can I get a session with you?

40:15.121 --> 40:15.955
Sure.

40:17.915 --> 40:19.417
Tell me what's on your mind.

40:30.344 --> 40:31.762
Oh, there you are.

40:33.180 --> 40:34.432
You should eat something.

40:34.515 --> 40:37.601
Gang-tae made egg soup. It's very good.

40:37.685 --> 40:42.148
But I... I like the rice bowl more,
so that's what I had.

40:47.194 --> 40:50.197
Oh, right. Is your head okay?

40:50.698 --> 40:54.827
I saw that evil woman
grab you by the hair yesterday.

40:56.287 --> 40:57.746
Did you lose a lot of hair?

41:01.750 --> 41:04.336
She tried to hurt you
because she didn't want you to be happy.

41:04.420 --> 41:06.797
She's evil. So evil.

41:10.050 --> 41:13.345
Right, I need to show you my homework.

41:13.429 --> 41:16.056
I practiced drawing
so many facial expressions.

41:16.140 --> 41:17.600
Do you want to see it?

41:17.683 --> 41:18.517
- Sang-tae.
- Yes?

41:23.105 --> 41:24.482
That homework...

41:25.566 --> 41:26.650
You don't need to do it.

41:28.652 --> 41:29.487
What?

41:30.696 --> 41:33.574
We won't publish the book.

41:33.657 --> 41:38.496
What? Why... Why not?
Why won't we publish it?

41:38.579 --> 41:39.830
Because I don't want to.

41:40.748 --> 41:44.418
And when Gang-tae is back
from the hospital,

41:44.960 --> 41:46.295
I want you guys to move out.

41:47.713 --> 41:49.673
I'm terminating our contract.

41:51.842 --> 41:54.929
If you... If you terminate the contract,

41:55.012 --> 41:57.848
the penalty goes up threefold.

41:57.932 --> 41:59.308
I'll pay you however much you want.

41:59.975 --> 42:01.393
Move out before the end of the day.

42:04.647 --> 42:05.981
Over my dead body.

42:08.192 --> 42:09.693
Over my dead body. I don't care.

42:09.777 --> 42:11.403
Over my dead body.
I don't care what you say.

42:11.487 --> 42:13.614
Over my dead body!

42:13.697 --> 42:15.199
Over my dead body. I'll win this fight.

42:15.282 --> 42:18.911
No way, I'm not moving out.
Over my dead body!

42:31.423 --> 42:32.508
To be honest,

42:35.928 --> 42:37.388
I'm not sure if I can handle it.

42:40.224 --> 42:41.183
Do Hui-jae...

42:43.811 --> 42:45.563
The things that woman said to me,

42:47.064 --> 42:49.567
her face, and the things that she did...

42:50.943 --> 42:52.361
Whenever I think about those things,

42:53.779 --> 42:55.364
my mom, who was killed unjustly,

42:56.699 --> 42:58.742
and my brother,
who saw that while hiding...

43:03.122 --> 43:04.873
I just can't get any of it out of my head,

43:09.503 --> 43:10.963
and I can't breathe.

43:15.509 --> 43:17.094
Despite that,

43:17.177 --> 43:19.054
I lied to Mun-yeong.

43:20.306 --> 43:23.267
I said that I could overcome all of it.

43:27.313 --> 43:28.314
But...

43:33.819 --> 43:34.903
Mun-yeong

43:36.238 --> 43:37.323
won't buy it.

43:43.203 --> 43:46.707
Being together torments you.

43:48.000 --> 43:51.587
But if you break up,
it'll be equally painful.

43:53.130 --> 43:55.257
If both options feel like death,

43:55.341 --> 43:57.176
wouldn't it be better to suffer together?

43:59.011 --> 44:00.179
Be honest with me.

44:01.221 --> 44:04.099
I bet you wanted to kill Do Hui-jae
when you were alone with her.

44:09.855 --> 44:11.815
Yes, kill me.

44:14.068 --> 44:16.278
- Yes.
- Then why didn't you kill her?

44:20.032 --> 44:21.200
Because

44:22.826 --> 44:24.078
I thought of Mun-yeong.

44:26.497 --> 44:29.166
Right, exactly.

44:29.833 --> 44:31.919
The one that torments you

44:32.002 --> 44:35.798
can also be the one to save you.

44:37.007 --> 44:38.801
You were about to explode,

44:39.885 --> 44:41.762
but she prevented you from blowing up.

44:56.819 --> 44:58.695
What is all this?

45:01.407 --> 45:04.743
Mun-yeong,
why on earth are you being like this?

45:04.952 --> 45:05.828
What do you think?

45:05.911 --> 45:07.704
I told you everything over the phone
yesterday.

45:07.788 --> 45:09.540
I'm not going to write anymore.

45:13.293 --> 45:14.336
Fine.

45:14.753 --> 45:17.548
I understand it's about time
you got tired of writing fairy tales.

45:18.006 --> 45:22.052
Then why don't we just switch
to a different genre?

45:24.888 --> 45:28.642
Yes, let's try a genre
that better suits your personality.

45:28.767 --> 45:32.104
What about a crime novel or a thriller?

45:32.563 --> 45:36.066
A horror novel? A martial arts fiction
or a tragic love story?

45:37.109 --> 45:37.943
Or...

45:38.277 --> 45:39.445
What about an erotic novel?

45:39.528 --> 45:40.446
I will retire.

45:41.029 --> 45:42.614
I don't want to write anymore.

45:42.698 --> 45:45.617
I'm just going to retire
and spend my time doing what I want.

45:46.660 --> 45:49.371
No. Don't say that, Mun-yeong.

45:49.997 --> 45:51.165
Gosh...

45:52.332 --> 45:55.919
If it's because of the mental shock
from the recent incidents,

45:56.795 --> 45:58.672
you can take about a year off and...

45:58.797 --> 45:59.840
Mr. Lee.

46:06.096 --> 46:07.139
There are

46:08.182 --> 46:10.517
no more stories that I want to write.

46:11.185 --> 46:12.352
That's why.

46:13.687 --> 46:15.439
And I'm going to sell this house.

46:15.522 --> 46:18.066
So stop hovering around me.

46:18.484 --> 46:20.694
Just go back to Seoul with Seung-jae.

46:21.111 --> 46:22.529
You're free now.

46:25.949 --> 46:27.618
No, no way.

46:28.494 --> 46:30.037
I can't even imagine

46:30.120 --> 46:31.914
SangSangESang Publishers
without Ko Mun-yeong.

46:31.997 --> 46:33.499
And without you,

46:33.624 --> 46:35.626
none of my visions will come true,

46:35.709 --> 46:37.794
so that freedom is completely useless.

46:38.003 --> 46:41.507
Mun-yeong, please. I'll be good to you.
Change your mind just this once.

46:41.590 --> 46:42.925
Stop whining.

46:43.133 --> 46:44.885
My head hurts
because I didn't get much sleep.

46:45.886 --> 46:47.387
I need to get some sleep, so get lost.

46:59.816 --> 47:03.070
I guess she's really made up her mind
to stop writing this time.

47:04.947 --> 47:09.076
Why don't we just find a different writer
to sign with and--

47:09.159 --> 47:12.913
Hey, do you think I'm being like this
to sell books and make money?

47:13.580 --> 47:14.414
Yes.

47:15.666 --> 47:17.251
Writing fairy tales

47:17.501 --> 47:20.796
is the only way
Mun-yeong can communicate with the world.

47:20.879 --> 47:22.881
It's the only way
she can talk and breathe.

47:22.965 --> 47:27.970
If she doesn't want to do that anymore,
it means she's just going to die.

47:44.319 --> 47:46.154
- Director O.
- Yes?

47:46.780 --> 47:49.283
You know how you asked me
to hang out with you earlier?

47:50.117 --> 47:51.952
What are you going to propose this time?

47:53.370 --> 47:56.748
Well, I'll come by from time to time.

47:57.666 --> 48:00.544
So in return, can I plant a tree
in the hospital garden?

48:00.627 --> 48:01.670
"A tree"?

48:02.212 --> 48:03.297
Sure. Why not?

48:04.464 --> 48:05.841
What kind of tree?

48:05.924 --> 48:08.802
It could be a walnut tree or a ginkgo--

48:08.885 --> 48:10.804
No, don't plant a ginkgo tree. They stink.

48:24.234 --> 48:25.485
I told you so!

48:26.236 --> 48:27.404
My baby.

48:55.932 --> 48:58.185
You seemed to be having a nightmare.

48:59.853 --> 49:01.396
Pack up and leave.

49:01.897 --> 49:03.106
I want you to leave today.

49:04.941 --> 49:06.735
I just need Mang-tae.

49:07.361 --> 49:08.904
I don't need Gang-tae anymore.

49:10.530 --> 49:11.657
Oh, right.

49:13.909 --> 49:16.703
You already told me
you don't want anyone to rely on you.

49:17.788 --> 49:20.499
So that's good. Now, hurry up and leave.

49:22.209 --> 49:23.210
Are you

49:26.630 --> 49:28.006
really going to live alone?

49:28.090 --> 49:31.385
I've been living alone all my life.

49:31.968 --> 49:35.305
People like me aren't able to live
among others.

49:35.931 --> 49:37.182
It's better to be secluded.

49:38.141 --> 49:40.352
- Why?
- Because that's how I was born.

49:42.938 --> 49:43.772
Mun-yeong.

49:45.232 --> 49:47.067
You can't live by yourself anymore.

49:48.443 --> 49:49.486
Why not?

49:50.070 --> 49:51.822
Because now, you know how it feels

49:52.948 --> 49:54.199
to feel warm at heart

49:55.867 --> 49:57.119
and to have a full stomach.

50:04.918 --> 50:05.877
So

50:07.129 --> 50:08.547
just admit it.

50:08.630 --> 50:09.840
Admit what?

50:12.259 --> 50:14.261
That you're just a little kid

50:15.011 --> 50:16.179
who wants to be loved.

50:29.568 --> 50:31.653
Cut the nonsense and just move out.

50:34.489 --> 50:37.325
Do you want me to tell you a story?

50:37.743 --> 50:38.910
No.

50:40.829 --> 50:42.414
A long time ago...

50:42.998 --> 50:44.124
Shut up.

50:45.208 --> 50:48.545
There lived two poor brothers
who cared for each other very much.

50:51.423 --> 50:54.885
One day, it was the harvest season,
so they both harvested rice.

50:55.552 --> 50:58.263
The older brother was worried
his little brother might run out of rice,

50:58.889 --> 51:01.975
so he secretly carried
a sack of rice at night

51:02.434 --> 51:04.436
and left it in front of
his little brother's house.

51:05.979 --> 51:10.025
The same day, the little brother
also carried a sack of rice

51:10.567 --> 51:12.652
and put it in front of
his older brother's house

51:13.653 --> 51:16.740
thinking that his older brother might
need more due to his big family.

51:17.657 --> 51:19.242
When they woke up the next day,

51:19.326 --> 51:23.121
they both noticed that they still had
the same amount of rice as before.

51:25.123 --> 51:27.250
The two brothers thought it was strange.

51:27.876 --> 51:30.253
So they did the same thing that night
and left a sack of rice

51:31.004 --> 51:32.380
in front of each other's house.

51:35.258 --> 51:39.638
And that continued for days.

51:44.267 --> 51:46.186
Do you know
what the moral of this story is?

51:50.148 --> 51:51.817
"Siblings who care a lot about each other

51:52.609 --> 51:56.071
should live together so they won't
end up doing pointless work."

51:59.491 --> 52:00.492
It's funny, isn't it?

52:02.536 --> 52:03.703
What a joke.

52:04.287 --> 52:05.580
What kind of moral is that?

52:07.666 --> 52:09.000
My brother came up with it.

52:12.087 --> 52:13.088
Do you not like

52:15.757 --> 52:17.133
me and my brother?

52:20.846 --> 52:22.013
I know you do.

52:24.057 --> 52:25.016
Right?

52:27.561 --> 52:31.147
Let's not do anything
that will waste our time.

52:32.899 --> 52:34.442
I don't care where we live.

52:36.278 --> 52:37.654
I just want us to live together.

52:39.656 --> 52:40.615
Okay?

52:52.377 --> 52:53.503
Mun-yeong.

52:58.341 --> 52:59.384
Answer me.

53:01.845 --> 53:03.805
Can we talk?

53:05.390 --> 53:07.851
Will you stop being so stubborn?

53:09.394 --> 53:11.354
Did you just yell at me?

53:16.026 --> 53:16.860
No.

53:17.652 --> 53:20.947
I think my voice tends to sound louder

53:21.698 --> 53:23.909
in this room.

53:28.580 --> 53:30.415
I'll leave you to get some rest
if you're tired.

53:33.793 --> 53:34.753
Get some rest.

53:54.314 --> 53:56.066
Why not?

53:56.399 --> 53:58.860
- Cancer.
- Cancer?

53:59.527 --> 54:00.904
- You heard me.
- Yikes!

54:00.987 --> 54:02.072
It's too late.

54:04.407 --> 54:06.034
Did... Did you tell her?

54:08.119 --> 54:08.954
Yes.

54:09.704 --> 54:12.374
But I think I only made it worse.

54:14.417 --> 54:16.544
Did... Did you follow my instructions?

54:18.296 --> 54:21.758
I told her that siblings who care
a lot about each other

54:22.342 --> 54:25.011
should live together so they won't
end up doing pointless work.

54:25.553 --> 54:27.806
I... I bet you made it sound boring.

54:28.640 --> 54:31.643
Some people have a way
of making things sound really boring.

54:32.894 --> 54:34.479
Gang-tae, you're so boring.

54:38.024 --> 54:41.027
- I'm going to die now!
- "I'm going to die now!

54:41.111 --> 54:43.697
- I have so much resentment and regret.
- I have so much resentment and regret.

54:43.780 --> 54:44.990
- There's so much I want to eat.
- There's so much I want to eat.

54:45.073 --> 54:46.658
- I feel so bad for myself!
- I feel so bad for myself!

54:46.741 --> 54:49.411
- My... My pitiful youth!"
- My... My pitiful youth!

54:49.494 --> 54:51.162
My gosh, this is so hard.

54:53.581 --> 54:55.166
- Whatever.
- You're not popular

54:55.250 --> 54:57.252
because you're so boring.

54:57.335 --> 55:00.547
Let's be honest.
BLACKPINK is the most popular.

55:00.630 --> 55:02.465
Let's be honest about that.

55:17.105 --> 55:18.815
Why are you alone? Did you call Mun-yeong?

55:18.898 --> 55:21.693
Yes, but she didn't respond.

55:21.776 --> 55:24.195
It was so rude of her not to reply.

55:26.573 --> 55:27.574
Hey.

55:27.949 --> 55:30.827
Come eat with us.
We have quail eggs and rolled omelet...

55:32.120 --> 55:33.163
Can we talk?

55:50.680 --> 55:51.848
When are you going to leave?

55:53.933 --> 55:55.101
You should eat first.

55:55.602 --> 55:56.686
You haven't eaten anything.

55:57.270 --> 55:58.688
Are you trying to be a live-in-cook?

55:59.606 --> 56:02.776
Go back to where you used to live.

56:04.861 --> 56:06.780
- We can't.
- Why not?

56:07.572 --> 56:10.325
The water pipe burst.

56:11.451 --> 56:13.870
- What?
- The entire place is flooded.

56:15.246 --> 56:16.623
It'll take days to fix.

56:41.106 --> 56:42.941
Hey, it's me.

56:43.983 --> 56:45.235
Can you talk right now?

56:49.155 --> 56:50.657
NURSES' OFFICE

56:52.033 --> 56:52.951
Ju-ri.

56:53.743 --> 56:55.537
Shouldn't we tell the patients

56:55.620 --> 56:57.789
that Director O is going to retire?

56:57.872 --> 57:00.041
I feel like they already know.

57:00.917 --> 57:02.794
"Things aren't very stable

57:02.877 --> 57:05.130
because people keep quitting.

57:05.338 --> 57:07.882
If we tell them now,
the patients will feel agitated."

57:08.716 --> 57:10.343
That's what Director O said.

57:11.094 --> 57:14.514
But shouldn't we at least plan
a retirement ceremony?

57:14.597 --> 57:17.308
Gosh, it's not an honorable retirement.

57:17.392 --> 57:19.185
I'm leaving because
I'm no longer qualified.

57:19.477 --> 57:21.312
You're done with your shift, right?

57:21.396 --> 57:22.522
Yes.

57:22.605 --> 57:24.399
Let's all go eat.

57:25.525 --> 57:26.985
I'll go after I make a phone call.

57:35.910 --> 57:36.828
What do you want?

57:36.995 --> 57:41.040
Mun-yeong, I'm really sorry,
but can you do me a favor?

57:41.166 --> 57:42.292
No, I can't.

57:42.750 --> 57:44.377
My mom is sick.

57:47.630 --> 57:51.551
She took the day off today
because she's really sick.

57:51.843 --> 57:53.970
I called her earlier,
and she didn't sound very well,

57:54.053 --> 57:55.472
so I'm really worried about her.

57:58.099 --> 58:01.561
I can't reach Sang-in and Seung-jae
because they went to a seminar,

58:01.644 --> 58:02.854
and I have a night shift today.

58:02.937 --> 58:05.106
Then ask Gang-tae.

58:06.441 --> 58:07.859
I'm really sorry.

58:08.943 --> 58:10.695
But can you go instead?

58:11.279 --> 58:12.447
I know she's old and all,

58:12.530 --> 58:15.158
but she'll feel more comfortable
around a woman.

58:16.034 --> 58:17.785
- Can you help?
- No, I can't.

58:17.869 --> 58:19.913
Why would you ask me
to take care of your mom?

58:38.806 --> 58:40.058
Hey, you're here.

58:46.314 --> 58:47.565
Are you really sick?

58:49.234 --> 58:50.735
You seem to have more energy than I do.

58:50.818 --> 58:53.821
When you're my age, you're always sick.

58:54.614 --> 58:56.241
My knees ache

58:56.324 --> 58:58.034
along with the joints in my arms and legs,

58:58.618 --> 59:00.453
so I can't even sleep at night. Oh, boy.

59:01.454 --> 59:04.624
Nam Ju-ri, that two-faced bitch.

59:04.707 --> 59:06.876
Don't badmouth my precious daughter.

59:06.960 --> 59:08.461
Now, come here and eat.

59:14.926 --> 59:15.843
Here.

59:17.720 --> 59:19.597
I heard you didn't eat for days.

59:20.890 --> 59:23.142
So I cooked scorched rice soup
instead of rice.

59:24.727 --> 59:25.728
Here.

59:29.857 --> 59:30.984
Sit down.

59:32.902 --> 59:36.906
Just go along with it and eat.

59:37.949 --> 59:40.201
Do you know how many people
were involved in planning this

59:40.285 --> 59:42.453
so we could put something
into that empty stomach?

59:49.043 --> 59:51.713
Hey, it's me.

59:52.463 --> 59:53.965
Can you talk right now?

59:54.048 --> 59:57.260
Why? What is it this time?

59:57.343 --> 59:59.929
You're starting to scare me.

01:00:01.723 --> 01:00:03.766
No, it's not that.

01:00:05.935 --> 01:00:08.730
This is a bit embarrassing,
but I need your help.

01:00:10.023 --> 01:00:11.566
What? "Embarrassing"?

01:00:12.191 --> 01:00:14.986
Then you should take
the afternoon off tomorrow, Mom.

01:00:15.320 --> 01:00:16.863
Okay, sure.

01:00:17.363 --> 01:00:21.451
Tell Gang-tae to send me a list
of Mun-yeong's favorite food via text.

01:00:23.244 --> 01:00:26.331
Mun-yeong hasn't been writing, eating,

01:00:26.414 --> 01:00:27.832
or going outside.

01:00:27.915 --> 01:00:30.460
I was so worried
that something might happen to her.

01:00:30.543 --> 01:00:33.046
My gosh, thank you guys so much.

01:00:33.129 --> 01:00:35.506
My goodness. We're not doing this for you.

01:00:35.590 --> 01:00:38.426
We're doing it because Gang-tae asked.

01:00:40.386 --> 01:00:42.930
Then I'll prepare something else

01:00:43.014 --> 01:00:45.099
other than food.

01:00:45.808 --> 01:00:46.809
Like what?

01:00:53.024 --> 01:00:56.402
Hey, Jae-su. It's me, Seung-jae.

01:00:56.944 --> 01:01:00.406
By any chance, do you have time
to chat tomorrow?

01:01:01.449 --> 01:01:02.450
Okay, bye.

01:01:04.452 --> 01:01:05.620
I think he likes me.

01:01:09.248 --> 01:01:10.333
I'm serious.

01:01:13.169 --> 01:01:14.462
My goodness.

01:01:16.339 --> 01:01:17.465
Sit down and eat.

01:01:20.134 --> 01:01:21.302
Sit down.

01:01:25.932 --> 01:01:26.933
There.

01:01:28.685 --> 01:01:29.852
Eat up.

01:01:38.152 --> 01:01:39.904
Shit, it's so damn hot!

01:01:44.117 --> 01:01:47.120
Why would you swear like that
with that precious mouth of yours?

01:01:47.203 --> 01:01:49.330
Blow on it to cool it down
and eat it slowly.

01:01:49.414 --> 01:01:50.873
You don't want to burn your mouth.

01:02:01.175 --> 01:02:03.010
You won't believe it.

01:02:04.303 --> 01:02:05.596
Last night,

01:02:06.180 --> 01:02:08.433
Gang-tae called Sang-in

01:02:09.475 --> 01:02:12.812
and asked him for help
so he could get you to eat something.

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:16.649
I'm pretty sure he felt bad
about calling me.

01:02:17.316 --> 01:02:19.861
I bet he couldn't dare ask me
to cook for you

01:02:19.944 --> 01:02:22.488
after how he rejected Ju-ri.

01:02:23.948 --> 01:02:25.950
But you eventually cooked everything.

01:02:26.033 --> 01:02:28.536
Exactly. I'm such a fool.

01:02:36.961 --> 01:02:37.962
Here.

01:02:38.838 --> 01:02:39.839
There.

01:02:48.765 --> 01:02:49.849
Why is everyone

01:02:53.519 --> 01:02:55.021
so nice to me?

01:02:57.732 --> 01:02:59.233
I'm not your family.

01:03:00.359 --> 01:03:01.360
Because you're pretty.

01:03:02.653 --> 01:03:05.990
You're pretty, you eat well,

01:03:06.574 --> 01:03:09.660
and it's nice how you like Gang-tae
for who he is

01:03:09.744 --> 01:03:12.580
even though he has nothing to offer.

01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:36.103
Gosh, I'm hungry.

01:03:36.270 --> 01:03:37.855
Can I also have some food?

01:04:05.716 --> 01:04:08.052
Is... Is this Mom's tree?

01:04:08.135 --> 01:04:09.011
Yes.

01:04:11.097 --> 01:04:13.015
Whenever we miss her,

01:04:13.724 --> 01:04:15.601
we just need to come here.

01:04:15.685 --> 01:04:18.145
Oh, I see.

01:04:20.773 --> 01:04:22.441
Mom... Mom.

01:04:23.317 --> 01:04:26.362
This... This is our new family photo.

01:04:26.445 --> 01:04:29.740
The girl in the middle is Mun-yeong.
She's pretty.

01:04:29.824 --> 01:04:31.409
She... She looks better with long hair.

01:04:31.492 --> 01:04:34.912
But Gang-tae cut her hair like this.

01:04:38.624 --> 01:04:39.667
Mom.

01:04:42.253 --> 01:04:43.087
I

01:04:44.547 --> 01:04:45.756
grew up well, didn't I?

01:04:50.469 --> 01:04:52.680
Yes, you grew up well.

01:04:53.764 --> 01:04:55.600
And so did I.

01:04:56.976 --> 01:04:59.854
Mom, I hope you also grow up
into a big tree.

01:05:01.606 --> 01:05:03.149
From now on,

01:05:04.358 --> 01:05:06.027
I'll take good care of Sang-tae,

01:05:07.987 --> 01:05:08.863
Mom.

01:05:09.363 --> 01:05:12.491
She... She didn't have you
so you could take care of me.

01:05:13.576 --> 01:05:14.410
You...

01:05:15.661 --> 01:05:18.080
You weren't born to take care of me.

01:05:19.248 --> 01:05:20.708
That's...

01:05:21.417 --> 01:05:24.128
That's not why Mom gave birth to you.

01:05:25.671 --> 01:05:28.257
Older brothers are supposed to
take care of younger brothers.

01:05:28.424 --> 01:05:30.635
And... And that's why I hit that bad woman

01:05:31.344 --> 01:05:33.095
on the back of her head.

01:05:33.179 --> 01:05:36.849
I... I protected you
while you were sleeping.

01:05:41.062 --> 01:05:42.063
You're right.

01:05:43.898 --> 01:05:45.149
You were born

01:05:46.317 --> 01:05:47.777
to protect me.

01:05:48.986 --> 01:05:53.157
Yes, but you're all grown up now,
so it's time you take care of yourself.

01:05:53.240 --> 01:05:55.785
I'm... I'm busy now.

01:05:55.868 --> 01:05:57.161
Bye, Mom.

01:06:02.875 --> 01:06:03.834
Mom.

01:06:06.337 --> 01:06:07.338
Did you hear that?

01:06:16.931 --> 01:06:17.932
Wait for me.

01:06:26.941 --> 01:06:28.985
I'll be honest with you.

01:06:29.068 --> 01:06:32.363
I sometimes think
he might be a psychopath.

01:06:32.446 --> 01:06:35.908
He's way too cold-hearted and indifferent.

01:06:35.992 --> 01:06:37.326
I agree.

01:06:37.743 --> 01:06:40.871
I really hate it how he sometimes
puts on a fake expression.

01:06:41.831 --> 01:06:43.833
I know, right? My gosh.

01:06:43.916 --> 01:06:46.293
On top of that, he's also out of his mind.

01:06:48.045 --> 01:06:50.256
Do you know what he said to me last time
at my restaurant?

01:06:51.799 --> 01:06:53.175
Serengeti.

01:06:54.844 --> 01:06:56.554
Serengeti.

01:06:56.637 --> 01:06:58.472
Do you even know where that is?

01:06:58.556 --> 01:07:00.516
At first, I thought he was
talking about spaghetti.

01:07:00.599 --> 01:07:04.145
Serengeti is a place in Africa.
It's all the way in Africa.

01:07:04.228 --> 01:07:07.523
He wanted to go there
when he doesn't even have a passport.

01:07:07.606 --> 01:07:09.025
He's crazy.

01:07:09.108 --> 01:07:10.860
Why is that crazy?

01:07:12.445 --> 01:07:13.279
What?

01:07:16.240 --> 01:07:18.868
Why is it crazy
that he wants to go to Serengeti?

01:07:18.951 --> 01:07:20.327
Why?

01:07:21.120 --> 01:07:22.580
My gosh, you startled me.

01:07:53.277 --> 01:07:54.737
My goodness.

01:07:56.822 --> 01:07:58.449
Did you go somewhere?

01:07:59.033 --> 01:08:00.284
Sang-tae.

01:08:01.035 --> 01:08:02.745
You reek of alcohol.

01:08:06.749 --> 01:08:07.750
Sang-tae.

01:08:09.585 --> 01:08:11.712
Can you ask Gang-tae

01:08:13.297 --> 01:08:16.550
what excuse he's going to use tomorrow
to stay here?

01:08:19.261 --> 01:08:20.846
I went to Ju-ri's house,

01:08:21.639 --> 01:08:23.390
and their water pipe was fine.

01:08:26.894 --> 01:08:28.854
Over my dead body.

01:08:30.523 --> 01:08:31.941
Do you have a death wish?

01:08:32.024 --> 01:08:35.945
What? Oh, here.
You need to check my homework.

01:08:36.862 --> 01:08:39.240
I told you not to bother.

01:08:39.532 --> 01:08:41.826
I'm done writing fairy tales.

01:08:42.284 --> 01:08:43.494
I'm going to stop.

01:08:44.620 --> 01:08:45.496
No.

01:08:46.330 --> 01:08:47.498
I'm going to retire.

01:08:48.541 --> 01:08:53.629
You... You need to check my homework
so I can become an illustrator.

01:08:53.712 --> 01:08:56.173
So... So check my homework.

01:08:56.757 --> 01:08:58.884
Gosh, you're so stubborn.

01:08:59.760 --> 01:09:04.890
If... If you don't write,
I'll publish a book with someone else.

01:09:05.057 --> 01:09:06.851
I... I want to keep drawing.

01:09:08.602 --> 01:09:12.189
My gosh, you have no loyalty.

01:09:12.940 --> 01:09:14.692
You're just going to work with whomever?

01:09:15.359 --> 01:09:18.154
No... No, not whomever.

01:09:18.237 --> 01:09:20.030
I'll be working with a real partner.

01:09:23.117 --> 01:09:25.619
Okay, fine. Let's take a look.

01:09:26.412 --> 01:09:29.123
They used to be stick figures.
Let's see how much you've improved.

01:09:33.627 --> 01:09:36.714
Take... Take a look.

01:09:37.798 --> 01:09:39.717
He looks happy.

01:09:41.969 --> 01:09:44.972
He... He smiled like this

01:09:45.055 --> 01:09:47.850
after he told me he likes someone.

01:09:47.933 --> 01:09:49.185
He smiled.

01:09:49.268 --> 01:09:54.023
This... This is how Gang-tae looks
when he's happy.

01:09:54.106 --> 01:09:57.067
Take... Take a look at this.

01:09:57.151 --> 01:10:02.198
It's... It's not fake. He's really happy.

01:10:02.281 --> 01:10:05.159
Gang-tae... Gang-tae looks happy.

01:10:05.242 --> 01:10:08.120
I drew him
because I saw it for the first time.

01:10:20.049 --> 01:10:22.134
Look. Right here.

01:10:28.057 --> 01:10:30.100
It's a happy expression.

01:10:30.476 --> 01:10:32.436
Why are you crying?

01:10:33.687 --> 01:10:35.022
Because it's beautiful.

01:10:38.025 --> 01:10:39.610
It's so beautiful.

01:10:43.989 --> 01:10:45.699
Do you want it?

01:10:48.244 --> 01:10:49.078
Yes.

01:10:50.371 --> 01:10:51.580
I want it.

01:10:53.832 --> 01:10:55.125
Can I have it?

01:11:03.259 --> 01:11:05.302
Here. I'll let you have it.

01:11:13.018 --> 01:11:17.731
I... I really want to publish
a fairy tale book.

01:11:19.233 --> 01:11:22.987
I... I want to take my book
and show it to my mom.

01:11:23.070 --> 01:11:25.030
I want to tell her I'm an illustrator now.

01:11:31.912 --> 01:11:32.746
Your mom?

01:11:33.455 --> 01:11:37.793
Yes, we planted a tree for her
at OK Psychiatric Hospital.

01:11:38.377 --> 01:11:39.586
My mom's tree.

01:12:08.324 --> 01:12:09.241
I'm sorry.

01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:14.079
I'm so sorry.

01:12:28.052 --> 01:12:29.011
I

01:12:30.095 --> 01:12:31.138
followed you.

01:12:35.184 --> 01:12:37.102
Your hobby is to kidnap people.

01:12:38.979 --> 01:12:40.606
My hobby is to tail people.

01:12:47.196 --> 01:12:48.238
Do you think that's funny?

01:12:52.576 --> 01:12:53.994
I might not be funny.

01:12:58.165 --> 01:12:59.750
But I do want to impress you.

01:13:05.964 --> 01:13:07.716
I'll keep trying.

01:13:09.802 --> 01:13:10.803
I'll do everything I can

01:13:12.763 --> 01:13:14.431
to overcome what happened

01:13:15.808 --> 01:13:17.267
and cope with it.

01:13:19.853 --> 01:13:20.771
So please

01:13:22.022 --> 01:13:23.482
stop pushing me away.

01:13:24.733 --> 01:13:25.943
Let me stay by your side.

01:13:27.778 --> 01:13:28.612
Please?

01:13:44.336 --> 01:13:45.295
Then what about this?

01:13:47.047 --> 01:13:48.173
How will you compensate for this?

01:13:56.056 --> 01:13:57.224
I'm sorry

01:13:58.559 --> 01:13:59.643
I made you get hurt.

01:14:15.284 --> 01:14:16.118
I love you!

01:14:29.089 --> 01:14:31.133
I love you, Mun-yeong.

01:14:46.190 --> 01:14:47.357
I love you!

01:14:48.817 --> 01:14:49.860
I said, I love you!

01:14:54.448 --> 01:14:56.200
I love you so much!

01:14:58.202 --> 01:15:00.037
I said I love you! Why are you leaving?

01:15:03.123 --> 01:15:03.957
Hey!

01:15:05.042 --> 01:15:06.168
I love you!

01:15:09.505 --> 01:15:10.756
Mun-yeong!

01:15:11.381 --> 01:15:12.466
Wait...

01:15:13.926 --> 01:15:14.927
Mun-yeong, I love you.

01:15:15.969 --> 01:15:18.680
- Shouldn't he get admitted?
- I love you! Will you please stop?

01:15:18.764 --> 01:15:21.099
Mr. Moon has changed so much.

01:15:21.850 --> 01:15:23.310
Love changes people.

01:15:39.868 --> 01:15:40.702
Mun-yeong.

01:15:43.205 --> 01:15:44.122
I love you.

01:15:44.665 --> 01:15:47.042
Is that not it? Is it something else?

01:15:47.876 --> 01:15:49.044
Will you please say something?

01:15:50.087 --> 01:15:52.798
If you tell me you love me one more time,
I might just...

01:16:01.640 --> 01:16:02.849
You might just what?

01:16:07.729 --> 01:16:08.564
Do this?

01:17:37.361 --> 01:17:39.946
I want to become a real illustrator.

01:17:40.030 --> 01:17:40.864
A real one.

01:17:40.947 --> 01:17:42.824
No. You can't see it.

01:17:42.908 --> 01:17:44.493
- Get out.
- Why am I an outsider?

01:17:45.994 --> 01:17:47.954
They're publishing a fairy tale together

01:17:48.038 --> 01:17:49.831
so I have been ostracized.

01:17:51.458 --> 01:17:54.127
How long do you think
they will stay with you?

01:17:54.628 --> 01:17:56.380
You will never be able to erase me.

01:17:57.964 --> 01:17:59.299
This is my last manuscript.

01:18:00.550 --> 01:18:02.594
You can discard it or publish it.

01:18:02.678 --> 01:18:03.553
It's up to you.

01:18:03.637 --> 01:18:06.139
I really hope you're not in pain anymore.

01:18:06.765 --> 01:18:07.974
I'm sorry.
